Package: fractalsql-druid
Version: @VERSION@
Section: database
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Depends: default-jre-headless (>= 2:1.17) | java17-runtime-headless | java21-runtime-headless | java25-runtime-headless, libcurl4, libssl3
Maintainer: FractalSQLabs <ops@fractalsqlabs.io>
Homepage: https://github.com/FractalSQLabs/fractalsql-druid
Description: FractalSQL for Apache Druid: the extension, fractalsqld and the MCP server
 The Druid extension JAR (SQL functions, the FRACTAL_SEARCH aggregate and the /fractalsql
 service endpoints), fractalsqld (the reasoning, embedding and enterprise service that runs
 beside the Druid brokers), and fractalsql-druid-mcp (a Model Context Protocol server for
 Druid).
 .
 After installation: copy /usr/lib/fractalsql-druid/extensions/fractalsql-druid into
 Druid's extensions directory, add "fractalsql-druid" to druid.extensions.loadList, edit
 /etc/fractalsql/fractalsqld.conf (the signing key, /etc/fractalsql/hmac.key, is created on
 install), and start the service: systemctl enable --now fractalsqld. How to start the MCP
 server: /usr/share/doc/fractalsql-druid/mcp/RUN.txt.
